<h3 id="sbi-in-physics-and-astronomy-kick-off-event">SBI in Physics and Astronomy Kick-off Event</h3>

<p>Simulation-based inference (SBI) is playing an increasingly important role in particle physics, astrophysics and cosmology. Various research groups at Science Park are playing an internationally visible role in its development and application, but are currently somewhat disconnected from each other. To connect students and researchers who are using or developing SBI, or who are just interested in getting involved, we aim to establish a regular meeting series, with a shape, form and content tuned to your needs or interests.</p>

<p>In order to kick this off and get to know each other, we plan a
<strong>Amsterdam Science Park SBI in Physics &amp; Astronomy Kick-off event</strong> (late October/early November)</p>

<p>The event will be half day, with longer and shorter presentations, and with ample time for discussions. The goal of the event is to provide a first quick overview of ongoing and planned activities, set the context, and conclude with concrete plans for events during the academic year.</p>

<div class="alert-box info ">
<ul>
  <li>Date: TBA; late October/early November 2026</li>
  <li>Location: TBA</li>
</ul>
</div>

<p><strong>Draft agenda:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>2-3 shorter overview talks about opportunities and open challenges of applying SBI in particle physics, astronomy and astroparticle physics/cosmology</li>
  <li>coffee break</li>
  <li>breakout discussions on various SBI topics</li>
  <li>Joined discussion to converge on topics and format for regular meetings about SBI</li>
</ul>

<p>We aim for a joint lunch before/after the event.</p>

